---
import Button from './Button.astro';
---

<section id="why" class="section story">
  <div class="container story-grid">
    <div class="story-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">
        We get it,
        <br />
        <span class="hl-teal">rolling updates ruin everything</span>
      </h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You have probably watched a routine security update take down your graphics
          driver, your audio pipeline, or the one package you actually cared about. Then
          you spent a Saturday putting it back together.
        </p>
        <p>It is not your fault.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>
            Most Linux distributions are mutable trees patched in place, and that model
            makes every update a gamble. There is no "before" to go back to, only
            whatever survived.
          </strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Atomic images flip the model. The root filesystem is read-only and versioned.
          An update writes a new snapshot alongside the old one, reboots into it, and if
          anything is wrong you select the previous deployment from the bootloader.
          Recovery becomes a menu entry instead of a reinstall.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is the entire idea. Everything else here — the image catalogue,
          reproducible layers, pinned digests — is in service of making the rollback
          boring.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-actions">
        <Button href="#faq" variant="teal">
          How it works
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="story-aside" aria-label="The difference in one line">
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="compare-pane compare-old">
          <h3 class="compare-title">Classic distro</h3>
          <ul class="compare-list">
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> Mutated in place
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> One broken state
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> Recovery means reinstall
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> "Works on my machine"
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="compare-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          →
        </div>

        <div class="compare-pane compare-new">
          <h3 class="compare-title">Atomic image</h3>
          <ul class="compare-list">
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Snapshots, not patches
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Previous deployment kept
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Roll back at boot
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Pinned, signed digests
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="story-aside-note">
        Same hardware. Same kernel. Completely different failure model.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story {
    background: var(--ink-raised);
    border-block: 2px solid var(--ink-line);
  }

  .story-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .story-copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    justify-items: start;
  }

  .hl-teal {
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .story-actions {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* --- compare card -------------------------------------------------------- */

  .story-aside {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    background: var(--ink);
    border: 3px solid var(--paper);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-paper-md);
  }

  .compare {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .compare-pane {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink-line);
  }

  .compare-old {
    background: #1a1520;
    border-color: #3a2b33;
  }

  .compare-new {
    background: #0f2a26;
    border-color: #1d4a42;
  }

  .compare-title {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .compare-old .compare-title {
    color: var(--coral);
  }
  .compare-new .compare-title {
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .compare-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .x {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--coral);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .tick {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--green);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .compare-arrow {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .story-aside-note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .story-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
    }

    .story-aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
